Hope cntr-L works this time

Well, I just got killed for the first time.  I was a knight.  about dlvl
15 or so I was getting a telepathic signal from King Arthur.  I found
a magic portal and presto! I was at Camelot.  Some horrible critter
had apparently attacked the castle.  I found the king (along with a 
peaceful minotaur and djini -- no wishes).  I chatted with the King.
He seemed rather pissed at me.  Said I had dishonored him and the
realm (or some such blather) and that I should return when I had done
penance (sp?).  Next thing I know, I'm back in the dungeon on the level
with the portal.  So I think to myself that maybe I should find a lawful
altar and sacrifice a bunch of crap.  Found one, sacrificed, got four leaf
clovers and a feeling of reconciliation, when back to the portal, back to
Camelot and his royal hiny (er, um, highness) is still pissed.  Well,
there are some stairs that lead done in Camelot, so I try these, but
"a mysterious force" prevents me from descending.  Not sure if this
is a bug or if I can't descend because King A. is pissed.  Anyway, a pretty 
good first game. >60,000 points, boots of speed gauntlets of power.
Lawful altars do not make holy water any more (at least not by just 
dropping water onto them.  I like the message you get when you first
enter the rogue level, can't remember it exactly, but has to do with,
you enter a region that looks very old.  The characters are different
for this level too.  For example a "%" donotes stairs, up and down.  
The only new monster I met was a mind flayer.  Tried to suck out my
brains I imagine, but My helmet stopped it.  I seemed to lose a lot
of total hit points,  I ate a bunch of poisonous corpses without poison
resistance, maybe this is a new feature (lose hp when eating poisoned
stuff).  I finally did get p.r. after eating several killer bees in 
a hive.  

If anyone finds out what to do for penance to make the old man happy,
let me know.  Pretty fun game so far.

